# Environment Variables Template
#
# This file is an inventory of every environment variable the code actually
# reads, grouped by the feature that consumes it. Copy it to `.env.local` and
# fill in only what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Rules:
#   - Never commit a real value. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not.
#   - Entries marked [SECRET] must never be committed, printed, or exposed.
#   - Entries are marked (required) or (optional); when optional, the comment
#     gives the exact value the code falls back to.
#   - Where a variable is read but currently has NO effect, that is stated
#     rather than implied, so nobody tunes a dead setting.
#
# The variable NAMES below are verified against the source by the command in
# CONTRIBUTING.md. The descriptions, fallbacks and citations are maintained by
# hand - please correct them if you find one stale.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the alian_structure-api backend (lib/api.ts:5).
# (optional) falls back to http://localhost:3001
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search (Algolia)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The client is built at module scope with '' fallbacks
# (features/agent-discovery/services/searchService.ts:4-8) and nothing
# validates it: algoliasearch('','') and client.initIndex('') both return
# without throwing, so a missing configuration is NOT caught at startup.
# (required) for agent discovery search. Falls back to '' - searches then fail
# against Algolia rather than the app refusing to boot
ALGOLIA_APP_ID=
# [SECRET] Algolia admin key, read at module scope (searchService.ts:5).
# (required) for agent discovery search. Falls back to ''
ALGOLIA_API_KEY=
# Name of the Algolia index the search service queries (searchService.ts:8).
# (required) for agent discovery search. Falls back to ''
ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage (IPFS / NFT.Storage)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [SECRET] NFT.Storage API token (lib/ipfs.ts:20). An nft.storage token is a
# WRITE credential.
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is wrong for a secret: Next.js inlines any
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into whichever client bundle reaches it.
# NOT EXPOSED TODAY, and that is worth knowing precisely: the only importer of
# uploadToIPFS is components/AgentMintingWizard.tsx, and nothing in the repo
# imports or renders that component, so no shipped bundle contains it. The other
# two importers of lib/ipfs (lib/agentMetadataSchema.ts:1, lib/stellar.ts:5)
# import only the AgentMetadata type, which TypeScript elides because it is used
# only in type position (lib/agentMetadataSchema.ts:15, and never in stellar.ts).
# The risk is prospective - wiring the wizard up under the current name would
# publish the token to every browser.
# (optional) for the rest of the app. Falls back to '' - nothing reads it today.
NEXT_PUBLIC_NFT_STORAGE_TOKEN=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web push notifications
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VAPID public key (base64url) used to request a push subscription
# (lib/notifications.ts:148). Not a secret. Without it, subscribe() rejects and
# the rejection is caught at lib/notifications.ts:152-154, which logs and returns
# null - and a browser without push support throws at :140 instead.
# (optional) for the rest of the app. Falls back to ''
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stellar networks (lib/stellar-constants.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Horizon endpoint per network. (optional) fallbacks:
#   mainnet  -> https://horizon.stellar.org
#   testnet  -> https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
#   futurenet -> https://horizon-futurenet.stellar.org
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_MAINNET_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_TESTNET_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_FUTURENET_URL=

# Stellar network passphrase per network. (optional) fallbacks:
#   mainnet   -> Public Global Stellar Network ; September 2015
#   testnet   -> Test SDF Network ; September 2015
#   futurenet -> Test SDF Future Network ; October 2022
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE_MAINNET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE_TESTNET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE_FUTURENET=

# Which network the app connects to on first load. (optional) falls back to
# "mainnet"; any value outside mainnet|testnet|futurenet also falls back to
# "mainnet" (lib/stellar-constants.ts:46).
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_STELLAR_NETWORK=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version registry
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contract id of the on-chain version registry
# (features/agent-versioning/services/versionRegistry.ts:7).
# (optional) falls back to '' - getContractVersions() then returns []
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERSION_REGISTRY_ID=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent telemetry
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WebSocket URL of the local telemetry stream
# (features/agent-telemetry/hooks/useTelemetryWebSocket.ts:23).
# (optional) omit to use the built-in mock stream in the dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEMETRY_WS_URL=
# Port the local dev telemetry broadcaster listens on (scripts/telemetry-ws-server.mjs:9,
# started with `npm run telemetry:ws`).
# (optional) falls back to 3456
TELEMETRY_WS_PORT=3456


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Metrics dashboard (optional - omit to use built-in mock metrics)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These two are resolved in order by getBaseUrl() at lib/metrics/prometheus.ts:30-36:
# METRICS_OTEL_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL is checked first (:31), then METRICS_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL
# (:33), and the mock is used only when BOTH are unset (:35). Setting one does not
# disable the other, and leaving one unset does not by itself select the mock.
# Imported only by the server routes app/api/metrics/panel/route.ts:4 and
# app/api/metrics/panels/route.ts:3, so never shipped to the browser.
#
# Prometheus HTTP API base URL (server-side only; do NOT prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC)
# Example: http://localhost:9090
# (optional) read at lib/metrics/prometheus.ts:33; consulted only when
#   METRICS_OTEL_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL is also unset
METRICS_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL=
#
# If using OpenTelemetry Collector, you can point this at its Prometheus exporter
# Example: http://localhost:9464
# (optional) read at lib/metrics/prometheus.ts:31; takes precedence over
#   METRICS_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL when both are set
METRICS_OTEL_PROMETHEUS_BASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Appended as a `?v=` query parameter to the request URL - the code builds
# `${request.url}?v=${buildId}` - by the four `cacheKeyWillBeUsed` callbacks in
# the `runtimeCaching[i].options` entries of the `pwa` object
# (next.config.js:32,50,68,86). Falls back to Date.now() per
# request.
# NO EFFECT TODAY: that block lives in the `pwa` object, and next-pwa is a
# dependency but is never imported or applied - next.config.js:157 exports the
# config unwrapped, so the object is inert. public/sw.js and public/manifest.json
# are hand-written statics with no buildId. Set it only if next-pwa is wired up.
# (optional) falls back to Date.now().toString() per request
BUILD_ID=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Framework (set by Next.js - do not set by hand)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read once at next.config.js:9 as the `disable` flag of the same unwired
# `pwa` object, so like BUILD_ID it currently has no effect. Next.js sets
# NODE_ENV itself; leave it unset in .env.local.
# (optional) no fallback; Next.js always defines it
NODE_ENV=


# ===========================================================================
# NOT IMPLEMENTED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These eight are listed in README.md ("## Configuration" -> "Environment
# Variables", README.md:363-385) but NO source file reads them. They are
# collected here so the docs stop implying behaviour that does not exist. If
# you add support, move the entry into the feature section above and add it to
# this file's regeneration command.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_AFFILIATE
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_PWA
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_JWT_EXPIRY
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_RPC_URL
#   SESSION_STORAGE_KEY
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK was superseded by NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_STELLAR_NETWORK
# plus the per-network passphrase variables above. NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_RPC_URL has
# no env-driven successor at all: the rpcUrl values are hardcoded at
# lib/stellar-constants.ts:23,36. The README still documents both.
#
# Separately: NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_BETA_FEATURES was documented only in the
# previous version of THIS file (never in the README) and no code reads it, so
# it has been dropped rather than carried forward.
# ===========================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Follow-ups (not done here, tracked by this file)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. NEXT_PUBLIC_NFT_STORAGE_TOKEN should be renamed and read server-side before
#    anything renders the minting wizard. It is not leaked today only because
#    components/AgentMintingWizard.tsx is unreachable from every entrypoint; the
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix would publish the token the moment that changes. Renaming
#    alone is not enough either: lib/ipfs.ts has no server-side consumer, so the
#    upload has to move into an API route that reads the token server-side. That
#    is a code change, and it needs a migration note for anyone who has set it.
#    Either render the wizard or delete it - dead code carrying a credential is
#    how this becomes an incident.
# 2. BUILD_ID and NODE_ENV are inert because next-pwa is a dependency that is
#    never applied (next.config.js:157 exports the config unwrapped). Either wire
#    up next-pwa or delete the dead `pwa` object; until then both variables are
#    documented here only for completeness.
# 3. There is no startup validation, so a missing required variable still fails
#    at first use. A helper that warns on startup when a required variable is
#    absent would catch this earlier.
